# Juristid scheduled jobs on the Unraid host — EXAMPLE, not installed by anything.
#
# Installing this is a host change the owner approves: copy it to
# /boot/config/plugins/dynamix/juristid.cron, edit the two decisions below,
# run `update_cron`, and watch the first run of each line in its log.
# Everything the lines call is read-only except the backup, which writes one
# new set under the backup root and never deletes one.
#
# Decisions that must be made first (docs/open-decisions.md):
#   RPO     --rpo-hours / MONITOR_RPO_HOURS — how old the newest set may be
#   WHO     an Unraid notification agent (Settings > Notifications) — without
#           one, every alert below ends in the WebGUI bell and nobody is told
#
# Times are UTC (the host has no Tallinn zoneinfo). The nightly backup runs
# before the host's own 23:00 database dump and the 21:15/22:15 Lovable sync
# windows; the backup takes the host lock, so if a sync is running the backup
# refuses and says so in its log, and the daily monitor reports the age.
#
# Paths follow deploy/unraid-main/README.md; the monitor's environment file is
# deploy/unraid-main/cron/juristid-monitor.env.example, copied to
# /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/monitor.env (root, 600).

# Nightly backup set + age check (RPO is the decision; 24 is only an example)
45 20 * * * bash /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/repo/deploy/unraid-main/cron/juristid-backup-nightly.sh --repo /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/repo --data-root /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main --backup-root /mnt/user/backups/juristid-main --log-dir /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/backup-logs --rpo-hours 24 &> /dev/null

# Monitor: fast every 15 min, daily at 04:05, weekly on Monday 05:00
*/15 * * * * bash /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/repo/scripts/deploy/juristid-monitor.sh --tier fast --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/monitor.env --state-dir /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/monitor-state &> /dev/null
5 4 * * * bash /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/repo/scripts/deploy/juristid-monitor.sh --tier daily --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/monitor.env --state-dir /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/monitor-state &> /dev/null
0 5 * * 1 bash /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/repo/scripts/deploy/juristid-monitor.sh --tier weekly --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/monitor.env --state-dir /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/monitor-state &> /dev/null

# Register watch (docs/adr/0217): the open Teemad's Riigikogu bills and the
# ministry registers, nightly at 03:30 UTC (05:30 Tallinn), outside the backup,
# sync and release windows. It writes proposals only. The model step reads
# JURISTID_REGISTER_WATCH_AI=1 and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from its own file,
# config/register-watch.env (root, 0600), handed to this one exec — not
# juristid.env, so no service holds the key. The file must exist: `docker exec
# --env-file` refuses a missing one. Log: one line per run plus its errors; the
# runs are also in Haldus → Registrite jälgimine.
30 3 * * * docker exec --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/register-watch.env juristid-main-web python manage.py watch_registers >> /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/register-watch.log 2>&1

# New topics sweep (docs/adr/0218): drafts in the same registers that are not a
# Teema yet, for the «Uued eelnõud» page. At 04:20 UTC, after the register watch
# has finished (~16 min), so a draft a Teema already follows is left out. The
# sweep is on by default in production; the model step reads
# JURISTID_REGISTER_SWEEP_AI=1 and the key from the same env file.
# PROPOSED, NOT INSTALLED (docs/adr/0222 §5): the nightly Riigikogu cycle, after the register
# watch (03:30) and before the new-drafts sweep (04:20), so the shared Riigikogu ledger is not
# queued twice and an invitation's candidate exists before the sweep. It reads nothing unless
# JURISTID_RIIGIKOGU_MONITORING=1 is in register-watch.env (an owner decision with a release):
# 0 4 * * * docker exec --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/register-watch.env juristid-main-web python manage.py watch_riigikogu >> /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/riigikogu.log 2>&1
20 4 * * * docker exec --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/register-watch.env juristid-main-web python manage.py sweep_registers >> /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/register-sweep.log 2>&1

# The Government's commented agenda for Monitooring → «Valitsuse info» (docs/adr/0219):
# every half hour from Wednesday 12:00 to Thursday 12:00 Tallinn. In winter (UTC+2) that
# is Wed 10:00 UTC – Thu 09:59 UTC; in summer (UTC+3) move both lines an hour earlier. A
# week already read costs one query. Same env file (the model step and its key).
*/30 10-23 * * 3 docker exec --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/register-watch.env juristid-main-web python manage.py watch_government_agenda >> /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/government-agenda.log 2>&1
*/30 0-9 * * 4 docker exec --env-file /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/config/register-watch.env juristid-main-web python manage.py watch_government_agenda >> /mnt/user/appdata/juristid-main/government-agenda.log 2>&1
